About WPP Production

We are WPP Production - the unified global production company that brings together all of WPP's content producers, studios and craft experts into one connected organisation. We combine world-class human craft with next generation technology to originate, design, and deliver multi-channel content systems at scale. Built for borderless collaboration and powered by deep craft expertise, we are the production engine designed for today's always on, AI driven marketing world.

About WPP

WPP is the trusted growth partner for the world’s leading brands. We unite&nbsp;cutting-edge media intelligence and data solutions, world-class creativity, next-generation production, transformative enterprise solutions and expert strategic counsel&nbsp;in a single company -&nbsp;powered by exceptional talent and our agentic marketing platform, WPP Open,&nbsp;to help our clients navigate change, capture opportunity and deliver transformational growth. For more information, visit&nbsp; WPP.com .

A Hybrid working model

We believe the best work happens when we're together, fostering creativity, collaboration, and connection. That's why we’ve adopted a hybrid approach, with teams in the office around four days a week. If you require accommodations or flexibility, please discuss this with the hiring team during the interview process.

What does a Producer do at WPP Production? &nbsp;
 

The Role &nbsp;

The Audiovisual Producer are responsible for end-to-end project management, management of client relationships, agency relationships while leading a diverse and dynamic team to deliver. They play an important role in ensuring the smooth operations and delivery excellence of their clients’ projects. &nbsp;

He/she is responsible for delivering a completed project on time, on specification, and on budget. &nbsp;

The successful candidate will use their superior problem-solving skills, a passion for production, marketing and advertising and a desire to learn. They are highly organized and accountable leaders, who are able to build relationships and collaborate drawing on the expertise of Hogarth’s resources and capabilities.  &nbsp;

&nbsp;

Key Areas of Responsibilities &nbsp;

Communication &nbsp;

• The key day-to-day project contact with lower to mid-level clients and creative agencies &nbsp;

• Possesses accurate sense of client satisfaction level - facilitates the sharing client feedback with the team and management; sensitive to the client's needs and concerns &nbsp;

• Takes accountability to ensure that all team members are aware of timelines and deliverables &nbsp;
&nbsp;

Collaboration &nbsp;

• Develops and maintains high levels of team effectiveness (trust, communication, collaboration, productivity diversity and engagement) &nbsp;

• Serves as a mentor/coach to junior producers &nbsp;

  &nbsp;

Process &nbsp;

• Manage medium- to large-sized projects independently, from initiation through completion &nbsp;

• Serve as the production expert on audiovisual campaigns, working with cross-functional teams in a fast-paced agency Must be used to work with people in charge and in several projects at the same time. &nbsp;

• Manages client objectives, budget, expectations, deliverables and timelines and communicating changes/directions to team members &nbsp;

• Keeps projects on track through clear task lists, issue tracking, status reports, and meeting notes &nbsp;

  &nbsp;

Financial Management &nbsp;

